course: dictionary
lesson: 5911
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. The words around the word tell you which meaning the writer chose. Ask yourself: is this a thing to write with, a sign, or a person? «Owen wrote his name on his football in marker.» Here a marker is a pen, because you write with it.
explain: «Check the trail markers at every junction, so you stay on the right path.» Now marker means a sign that shows a place. The clues are trail and path. If the sentence is about finding your way, the marker is probably a sign, not a pen.
explain: The third meaning is a person or a player. In a football match, a marker is the player who stays close to an opponent. The clue is the game: if the sentence is about a game or a test, think of a person. Then try your meaning in the sentence to check it makes sense.
fact: A marker is a pen with a thick, coloured tip, also called a felt-tip pen or marker pen.
fact: A marker can be a sign or object that shows a place, like a mile marker on a road.
fact: A marker can be a person who marks pupils' work or tests.
fact: In sport, a marker is a player who guards an opponent in a game.
fact: «Permanent markers do not wash off, so they are used only on paper or with permission.»
exercise: «Owen wrote his name on his football in marker.» What is a marker here? | A sign showing a place on a road | *A felt-tip pen with a thick, coloured tip | A teacher who checks spelling | A player who guards an opponent
exercise: «Check the trail markers at every junction, so you stay on the right path.» What do trail markers show? | Names of the people who walk there | *Places on the path, so you stay on the right way | Colours for painting | Ways that rivers flow
exercise: In a football match, what is a marker? | A pen with a thick, coloured tip | Someone who sells the tickets | A sign at the side of the road | *A player who guards an opponent
test: Ms Lee is the marker for our spelling test. What is a marker in this sentence? | *A person who marks the work | A sign on a road | A pen for writing | A player who runs fast
test: «The mile marker said 12 miles to town.» What does a mile marker show? | A person who checks the road | A player in a game | A pen for drawing maps | *A place on a road, as a distance
exam: «Permanent markers do not wash off, so what should you do before you use one?» | Hide it in your bag | Use it anyway, because it is only a pen | Wash it off afterwards | *Check you have permission, and use it only on paper
